0,Shina language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shina_language,"Shina is an Indo-Aryan language of the Dardic group, spoken in the Karakorams and the western Himalayas: Gilgit, Hunza, the Astor Valley, the Tangir-Darel valleys, Chilas and Indus Kohistan, as well as in the upper Neelam Valley and Dras.",Shina,Indo-European
